1
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,248
I got you!

2
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:48,548
What?

3
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:52,051
What's in the blood that he vomited?

4
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,054
Toxin?

5
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:58,391
What is this? You're strong.

6
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,477
It's not fun at all.

7
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:05,482
Straw Doll Technique…

8
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:07,025
Resonance!

9
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:27,712
Just how many are there?

10
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:31,299
We should treat it
like a game of whack-a-mole.

11
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:35,553
Yes, just continue to exorcise it.

12
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,722
Don't leave any behind.

13
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:40,141
The opponent probably won't retaliate.

14
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:44,729
There are restrictions, but the wider
the range of the cursed technique,

15
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:47,482
the weaker the user's attack ability?

16
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,984
It's just hypothetical.

17
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,613
I was worried about the range
of the cursed technique,

18
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:56,032
the number of victims, and the barrier.

19
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:59,160
All of these will affect the user
in a subtractive way.

20
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:00,703
We're lucky.

21
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:03,706
We should be able to exorcise it quickly.

22
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:08,711
In that case, what comes after
might be the real threat.

23
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,304
Kugisaki!

24
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:20,306
I'm fine.

25
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,560
You continue on with the whack-a-mole.

26
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:27,605
Darn it!

27
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,816
Why is she always being taken away?

28
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,110
What was that anyway?

29
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:36,739
Was it a mole, or that thing?

30
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:38,950
It's neither of them!

31
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:41,244
Kugisaki?

32
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:44,330
-What? Is it my older brother?
-What?

33
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:47,834
-Hey!
-Let me join in!

34
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:49,711
What?

35
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,714
It ran away?

36
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,717
-Should I leave it?
-Hurry up! Chase after it!

37
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:59,721
Kugisaki and that guy left the barrier.

38
00:02:59,804 --> 00:03:03,725
She might run into someone
more troublesome than expected.

39
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,144
On the contrary,
it's a lot easier over here.

40
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:07,729
I can handle it by myself.

41
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:10,231
Prioritize Kugisaki. Hurry!

42
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:12,775
If the situation worsens,

43
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:15,737
you have to come out too.

44
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,915
Darn it! Don't touch me!

45
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:35,173
I see. It's a girl.

46
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:36,341
Oh, my.

47
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,593
I apologize.

48
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:44,307
-Gross!
-Both of our errand…

49
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:50,146
doesn't include killing sorcerers.

50
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:53,608
If you retreat, I will spare your life…

51
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,611
Young lady.

52
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,112
Errand?

53
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,405
What?

54
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:02,116
I thought we're both here
for the same reason.

55
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:06,162
Is he a Cursed Spirit, or a Curse User?

56
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,122
Speaking of which, what is this scent?

57
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,013
The last one!

58
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:29,435
The way to go around
behind them is too simple.

59
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:34,440
I told you,

60
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:36,192
it's too simple.

61
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:44,784
Did I exorcise all of them?

62
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:48,746
I don't have to worry
about Tsumiki for now.

63
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:51,207
What's left is…

64
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:01,968
It's still alive?

65
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:04,971
That wasn't the main body?

66
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:08,016
The barrier is still active.
What's going on?

67
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:16,774
Never assume that a Cursed Spirit
has a logical modus operandi.

68
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:20,695
Even so, there's something
that I don't understand.

69
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:27,994
Why didn't it start to kill
the marked humans until recently?

70
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:31,748
The first cursed death victim
was killed in June.

71
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:34,459
June?

72
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,966
Our goal is to…

73
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:45,428
recover Sukuna's finger.

74
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:22,733
Things that have an immense presence…

75
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,111
Things that are hiding…

76
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,281
Things that have been
absorbed by Cursed Spirits…

77
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,242
They are all resonating.

78
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:34,454
After being swallowed
by the Cursed Spirit,

79
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:37,165
the power of Sukuna's finger,
which was suppressed…

80
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:42,670
Its cursed energy was released
after obtaining Itadori's vessel in June.

81
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,799
Although they look the same,

82
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:50,761
compared to the one
at the detention center…

83
00:07:57,393 --> 00:07:58,394
It's much stronger!

84
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:09,655
Nue.

85
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:18,122
All right, I won again this time.

86
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,250
This is rare.

87
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:23,836
I'm surprised you want me
to train with you.

88
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,714
Are you feeling anxious
because of Yuji's growth?

89
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:30,676
Well, you can't solve anything
without making sacrifices.

90
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:34,222
You despise my help so much?

91
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:41,187
Megumi, I believe your strength
and potential are not weaker than Yuji.

92
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:44,649
It's just that your mental aspect
is holding you back.

93
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:49,028
Megumi, you don't know
how to bring out your best, right?

94
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,239
What?

95
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:54,283
Are you saying that I'm not doing my best?

96
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:57,411
No, I mean you don't know
how to try your best.

97
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:00,248
For example during the baseball game,

98
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,708
why did you make a sacrifice bunt?

99
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:10,883
You wanted Nobara to enter the base,
even though you'll get tagged out?

100
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:13,135
How admirable.

101
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:17,557
But if it's me or Yuji,
we will aim for a home run at any time.

102
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:22,520
I'm not saying that a bunt is not good.

103
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:26,941
As baseball is a team sport,
everyone has their own task.

104
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:30,236
But being a Jujutsu Sorcerer
is an individual job.

105
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:33,030
It's important to work
with other Jujutsu Sorcerers, too.

106
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:34,574
You're right.

107
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,868
But no matter how many allies you have,

108
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,080
you always die alone.

109
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:46,168
You're only trying to judge
and match those around you

110
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:50,965
instead of picturing
a stronger future version of yourself.

111
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:53,968
Is it because you have
an ace up your sleeve?

112
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:58,389
You think that at worst,
everything will be solved after you die.

113
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:03,894
Forget about me,
you won't even reach Nanami's level.

114
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:08,149
To die and then win,
and to die victoriously…

115
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,072
They are two completely
different things, Megumi.

116
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:20,036
Give it your all, and be more greedy.

117
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,881
How long have I been unconscious?

118
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,759
Was Divine Dog destroyed?

119
00:10:34,842 --> 00:10:37,011
No, was my cursed technique dispelled?

120
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:44,602
I guess this is the end for me.

121
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:51,025
Furube, yurayura…

122
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,116
It's a waste of your talent.

123
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,205
Forget it.

124
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:11,253
A Jujutsu Sorcerer's growth
never comes easy.

125
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,173
Back then…

126
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,008
Why did you escape?

127
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:20,346
Bring out the full potential
of the shadow.

128
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:23,974
Don't think about the specifics for now.

129
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:28,479
Release it while coagulating
your cursed energy.

130
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:34,527
Imagine a future version of myself
that has surpassed my limits!

131
00:11:35,152 --> 00:11:36,404
I'll show it to you!

132
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:38,364
With a firm base,

133
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:41,283
good sense, and imagination,

134
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:45,204
humans can change
with the slightest of events.

135
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,332
Domain Expansion.

136
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:56,298
Chimera Shadow Garden.

137
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:03,180
Although it's incomplete and ugly,

138
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,975
it's enough for now!

139
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,201
Be free…

140
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,163
to expand!

141
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:32,293
Expand the interpretation of…

142
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,338
the cursed technique!

143
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:05,743
Divine Dog's claws
were capable of harming that guy.

144
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:12,416
Of course,
it can penetrate you if you relax.

145
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,930
I'm so tired.

146
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:32,520
Where are the two of them?

147
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:37,191
Great.

148
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,693
This is great.

149
00:14:05,334 --> 00:14:08,712
Do you know the basis

150
00:14:09,922 --> 00:14:11,131
for human interaction?

151
00:14:11,215 --> 00:14:12,758
I don't.

152
00:14:13,384 --> 00:14:19,723
"I won't kill you,
so please don't kill me either."

153
00:14:19,807 --> 00:14:22,601
You can replace the word "kill"
with something else.

154
00:14:22,685 --> 00:14:26,355
In short, never cross any line
that violates someone else's dignity.

155
00:14:26,438 --> 00:14:30,401
Through this process,
mutual existence is realized.

156
00:14:30,943 --> 00:14:34,989
Breaking that rule, or acting arrogant
thinking that you have no need for it…

157
00:14:36,323 --> 00:14:38,325
You must feel great.

158
00:14:40,244 --> 00:14:43,080
If you do that to me again,
I'm going to kill you.

159
00:14:43,163 --> 00:14:46,041
What have we done to you?

160
00:14:46,125 --> 00:14:49,545
Use your brain.
Or else, you can go and die.

161
00:14:49,628 --> 00:14:50,546
Hey!

162
00:14:52,047 --> 00:14:55,050
I must make it clear
to Ikezawa and the gang today.

163
00:14:55,134 --> 00:14:58,095
I'm not their errand boy.

164
00:14:58,178 --> 00:14:59,889
All the best, Aida.

165
00:14:59,972 --> 00:15:03,058
But I may be the next target.

166
00:15:03,142 --> 00:15:05,311
Please don't do your best, Aida.

167
00:15:05,394 --> 00:15:07,021
Hey, you fatty!

168
00:15:07,104 --> 00:15:08,564
I will change my line.

169
00:15:08,647 --> 00:15:11,817
I'll ask them to make you
run errands from today!

170
00:15:11,901 --> 00:15:13,777
Are you going to betray your friend?

171
00:15:13,861 --> 00:15:15,029
Shut up!

172
00:15:15,779 --> 00:15:16,655
Megumi.

173
00:15:20,534 --> 00:15:23,954
Wait. Isn't that Ikezawa
and the rest lying over there?

174
00:15:24,705 --> 00:15:27,041
Didn't you promise not to fight again?

175
00:15:28,167 --> 00:15:29,960
Stop acting like my guardian.

176
00:15:31,545 --> 00:15:33,464
I hate bad guys.

177
00:15:37,134 --> 00:15:39,720
They use poor imagination and sensibility

178
00:15:40,304 --> 00:15:42,097
to live a good life for themselves.

179
00:15:42,806 --> 00:15:44,808
I'm not good at dealing with kind people.

180
00:15:45,809 --> 00:15:47,895
They forgive those bad guys…

181
00:15:49,313 --> 00:15:51,941
to make themselves seem virtuous.

182
00:15:54,526 --> 00:15:55,903
It makes me sick.

183
00:15:57,321 --> 00:15:59,406
Tsumiki is the typical kind person.

184
00:16:01,408 --> 00:16:02,493
It's gross.

185
00:16:06,705 --> 00:16:10,125
Sorry, I didn't expect it to spill.

186
00:16:11,585 --> 00:16:13,212
When I was in first grade,

187
00:16:14,213 --> 00:16:16,674
my father and Tsumiki's mother,

188
00:16:17,174 --> 00:16:19,802
our only family members,
fell in love with each other.

189
00:16:20,636 --> 00:16:22,137
And then they went missing.

190
00:16:23,931 --> 00:16:26,100
A white-haired stranger said this.

191
00:16:26,684 --> 00:16:32,064
Your father came from the Zenin family,
a well-known sorcerer clan.

192
00:16:32,147 --> 00:16:34,900
But he's a bad guy,
even I don't want to go near him.

193
00:16:34,984 --> 00:16:37,653
You're born after he ran away from home.

194
00:16:38,153 --> 00:16:39,780
Megumi.

195
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:43,325
You're your father's
biggest bargaining chip

196
00:16:43,409 --> 00:16:45,494
to go against the Zenin family.

197
00:16:46,161 --> 00:16:47,705
Are you mad?

198
00:16:49,123 --> 00:16:51,583
I solved the mystery
behind the missing money.

199
00:16:52,167 --> 00:16:54,712
It seems that I was sold
to that Zenin family.

200
00:16:55,713 --> 00:16:57,297
-Yes, I'm mad.
-What?

201
00:16:57,381 --> 00:16:59,967
-Especially at your insensible attitude.
-What?

202
00:17:01,176 --> 00:17:05,097
He was the one who helped
to solve the issue with the Zenin family.

203
00:17:05,723 --> 00:17:08,934
I was to work as a Jujutsu Sorcerer
in the future as a guarantee,

204
00:17:09,435 --> 00:17:13,605
in exchange for monetary support
from the school.

205
00:17:16,316 --> 00:17:18,235
What's the deal with Jujutsu Sorcerers?

206
00:17:18,318 --> 00:17:19,611
How stupid.

207
00:17:19,695 --> 00:17:22,281
Who do you want me to help?

208
00:17:22,364 --> 00:17:25,492
Tsumiki, what are you doing?

209
00:17:25,576 --> 00:17:27,286
Hello, Megumi!

210
00:17:27,369 --> 00:17:28,495
Nothing.

211
00:17:28,579 --> 00:17:33,292
Wait. Have you made up your mind
about the bravery test?

212
00:17:33,375 --> 00:17:36,128
I don't want to go but I'm worried,
so I'll come along.

213
00:17:36,670 --> 00:17:41,008
Tsumiki was cursed right after
I reached third year in middle school.

214
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:44,219
The origin and identity
of the curse were unknown.

215
00:17:44,303 --> 00:17:47,056
There were others who got cursed
similarly across the nation.

216
00:17:48,348 --> 00:17:51,435
The only thing we know
is that we know nothing.

217
00:17:51,518 --> 00:17:53,520
Tsumiki has been unconscious
since that day.

218
00:17:54,646 --> 00:17:57,107
If I have the ability to curse someone,

219
00:17:57,191 --> 00:17:59,568
I would rather think about those
who are dear to me.

220
00:18:00,235 --> 00:18:02,571
She always smiles and patronizes others.

221
00:18:03,155 --> 00:18:06,325
Being unable to forgive people
is not a bad thing.

222
00:18:06,408 --> 00:18:08,494
That's part of your gentleness.
Right, Megumi?

223
00:18:09,661 --> 00:18:11,872
She even acknowledged my nature.

224
00:18:13,332 --> 00:18:15,167
Even if Tsumiki is such a person,

225
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:17,961
she still gets angry when I hurt someone.

226
00:18:19,088 --> 00:18:20,964
I used to think that she's annoying.

227
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:24,343
I thought she's just a hypocrite.

228
00:18:25,886 --> 00:18:29,598
But now, I realize that I was wrong.

229
00:18:31,058 --> 00:18:33,185
Just like how I choose who to help,

230
00:18:33,769 --> 00:18:36,271
she was choosing to worry about me.

231
00:18:36,939 --> 00:18:40,109
I'm sorry, I was too naive.

232
00:18:40,859 --> 00:18:41,860
I will apologize.

233
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:46,365
Wake up, my stupid sister.

234
00:18:47,533 --> 00:18:50,953
Darn it. My head hurts so much.

235
00:18:52,329 --> 00:18:55,624
The Yasohachi Bridge curse
is just on top of the bridge.

236
00:18:56,291 --> 00:19:00,045
It didn't lift the curse
that made her unconscious, right?

237
00:19:02,297 --> 00:19:07,177
What's left is to let Itadori know
about this finger…

238
00:19:10,848 --> 00:19:12,891
FUSHIGURO FELL ASLEEP

239
00:19:15,227 --> 00:19:17,896
A strong presence appeared suddenly.

240
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:20,983
Did Sukuna's finger leave the barrier?

241
00:19:21,483 --> 00:19:25,445
If the one who eliminates
the vessel is a Jujutsu Sorcerer,

242
00:19:25,988 --> 00:19:27,906
then they are quite good.

243
00:19:28,490 --> 00:19:30,450
Even if they defeated the finger

244
00:19:30,534 --> 00:19:33,495
or the Special Grade Cursed Spirit,

245
00:19:34,496 --> 00:19:36,373
they couldn't have won unscathed.

246
00:19:36,957 --> 00:19:38,458
Are they all right?

247
00:19:40,794 --> 00:19:45,507
I slipped up. Please forget what I said.

248
00:19:45,591 --> 00:19:46,967
Stop right there!

249
00:19:47,551 --> 00:19:49,970
Is he going to get the finger?

250
00:19:50,762 --> 00:19:53,015
How dare you escape
with such a scornful method?

251
00:19:53,098 --> 00:19:55,517
Do you think you can
get rid of me like this?

252
00:19:56,018 --> 00:20:00,939
I feel inferior about my back,
so I'm warning you.

253
00:20:01,023 --> 00:20:02,482
If you look at my back,

254
00:20:02,566 --> 00:20:03,942
-I'm going to kill--
-What?

255
00:20:04,526 --> 00:20:05,444
Kugisaki.

256
00:20:05,527 --> 00:20:06,945
Oh, it's my older brother.

257
00:20:07,029 --> 00:20:09,448
You…

258
00:20:09,531 --> 00:20:14,578
You saw it, didn't you?

259
00:20:14,661 --> 00:20:18,332
-Who is this? I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry, brother! I didn't mean to!

260
00:20:18,415 --> 00:20:21,752
I'm going to kill you!

261
00:20:26,423 --> 00:20:28,717
Then why do you dress like this?

262
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,802
So that's where
the strange smell came from.

263
00:20:30,886 --> 00:20:33,013
Otherwise, it will feel stuffy.

264
00:20:33,096 --> 00:20:36,892
Rot Technique, Maximum…

265
00:20:39,603 --> 00:20:40,979
Wing King!

266
00:20:42,314 --> 00:20:45,859
I'm going to kill you.

267
00:22:16,742 --> 00:22:17,951
-Juju Stroll.
-Juju Stroll.

268
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:24,708
Mr. Gojo! Kugisaki!

269
00:22:25,375 --> 00:22:27,252
Shut up.

270
00:22:27,336 --> 00:22:29,838
It's so hot right now, I can't move.

271
00:22:29,921 --> 00:22:31,965
A girl approached Fushiguro!

272
00:22:33,633 --> 00:22:35,052
Formation B!

273
00:22:35,135 --> 00:22:36,136
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir!

274
00:22:37,846 --> 00:22:40,474
-Fushiguro!
-Fushiguro!

275
00:22:40,557 --> 00:22:42,225
Who is that girl?

276
00:22:42,309 --> 00:22:44,603
Did you forget the night
we drank together?

277
00:22:44,686 --> 00:22:46,813
You said you're happiest
when you're with me.

278
00:22:46,897 --> 00:22:48,774
-Is it a lie?
-You didn't forget, did you?

279
00:22:48,857 --> 00:22:52,486
-Remember!
-Seriously, what's wrong with you guys?

280
00:22:53,278 --> 00:22:57,240
Please don't touch him casually,
you sly cats!

281
00:22:57,324 --> 00:23:03,163
Megumi is going to practice violin
with me later.

282
00:23:04,081 --> 00:23:05,916
Let's go back, Megumi.

283
00:23:06,541 --> 00:23:09,920
Today, you must master
"Twinkle Twinkle Little Star."

284
00:23:10,504 --> 00:23:13,048
It's okay. Don't mind them.
Please go ahead.

285
00:23:13,131 --> 00:23:14,800
The station is just right ahead.

286
00:23:14,883 --> 00:23:16,301
Thank you.

287
00:23:16,384 --> 00:23:17,302
-What?
-What?

288
00:23:17,844 --> 00:23:20,138
So what were you guys up to?

289
00:23:20,722 --> 00:23:23,058
Can you not humiliate me?

290
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:27,813
Explain it to me!

291
00:23:29,981 --> 00:23:30,816
It hurts!
